// AIDL IPC surface
public interface IFlagService extends IInterface {
    boolean isFlagEnabled(String userId, String flagKey) throws RemoteException;
    List<FeatureFlag> getAllFlags(String userId) throws RemoteException;
}

// Isolated process service
public class FlagEngineService extends Service {
    private final IFlagService.Stub mBinder = new IFlagService.Stub() {
        @Override
        public boolean isFlagEnabled(String userId, String flagKey) throws RemoteException {
            return flagEngine.isEnabled(userId, flagKey);
        }
    };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design cross-process, low-latency audio paths on Android, including security and performance.

## Key Concepts
- Real-time audio path with AAudio
- Cross-process IPC via AIDL
- android:process and android:isolatedProcess
- Shared memory (ashmem) for zero-copy buffers
- Remote config for per-user audio chains; Keystore encryption
- Performance tests: latency, jitter, power

## Code Example
```java
// Pseudo AIDL surface sketch
interface IAudioChain {
  void setConfig(in Config cfg);
  void start();
  void stop();
  void process(in ByteBuffer inBuf, out ByteBuffer outBuf);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure audio latency in the real-time path under Doze?
- What trade-offs exist between ashmem vs. shared memory mappings for buffers?

